{
  "tutorial": {
    "id": 4260,
    "version": 1,
    "type": "course",
    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "Using True and False",
    "descriptionContent": "Learn what true and false values are in programming.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17161,
        "title": "Booleans",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145202,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>There's a special value that's <em>neither</em> a string <em>nor</em> a number: <code>true</code>.</p><p>There are no quotes around it, and it's not a numeric value.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145203,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>true</code> is great for situations like checking if a game setting is enabled.</p><p>Display <code>true</code> in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"46\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Sound enabled&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145204,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can store <code>true</code> in a variable just like a string or a number.</p><p>Store <code>true</code> in a variable and display it in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"49\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameRunning = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(gameRunning);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>true</code>, followed by <code>gameRunning</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145205,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>false</code> is another special value and the opposite of <code>true</code>. We can use it like <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145206,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Save the value <code>false</code> in the variable <code>status</code> and display <code>status</code> in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"var\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"49\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"69\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Player alive&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(status);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>false</code>, followed by <code>status</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145207,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's a good use for the values <code>true</code> and <code>false</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Showing if a game setting is switched on or off</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Storing values from one to five</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Showing if a game setting is switched on or off.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145208,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why is <code>false</code> not a string?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" autoPlay = \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">There are no quotes around it</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It's stored inside a variable</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">There are no quotes around it.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145209,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Pick the one that's best for showing that a player has no more lives.</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>const hasLives = false;</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>const hasLives = true;</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>const hasLives = false;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145210,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why is <code>\"false\"</code> not the same as <code>false</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">There are quotes around it, so <code>\"false\"</code> is a string</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"false\"</code> and <code>false</code> are the same</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">There are quotes around it, so <code>\"false\"</code> is a string.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145211,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Show the status of the auto-play setting by displaying <code>false</code> in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"44\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Auto-play&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>console</code> followed by <code>.</code> and then <code>log</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>false</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145212,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the variable <code>autoSaveGame</code> and store <code>true</code> inside it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"25\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" autoSaveGame = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>autoSaveGame</code>, and finally <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145213,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Disable friendly fire by creating the variable and storing <code>false</code> in it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;false&quot;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" friendlyFire = \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>friendlyFire</code>, followed by <code>false</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145214,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Adjust the auto-play settings by coding <code>true</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"21\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" autoPlay = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17162,
        "title": "Negating Values",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145215,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A <code>!</code> sign in front of <code>true</code> makes the expression result in <code>false</code>. If the player is not alive, they are defeated.</p><p>The <code>!</code> sign is the <strong>negation operator</strong>. It turns values into their <strong>opposite</strong>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145216,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we change a value to its opposite with <code>!</code>, we negate it.</p><p>Put a <code>!</code> sign before <code>true</code> to change its value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"17\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(!\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!</code>, followed by <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145217,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>!</code> operator before <code>false</code> changes its value, too. If a level is not locked, it has to be unlocked.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"13\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(!\" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!</code>, followed by <code>false</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145218,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use the <code>!</code> operator with variables to negate the values they store.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"40\" endIndex=\"41\" /><option startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"54\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerIsAlive = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(!playerIsAlive);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!</code>, followed by <code>playerIsAlive</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145219,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can save a whole negation in another variable, too.</p><p>Create the variable <code>playerIsDefeated</code> and use <code>!</code> to change <code>playerIsAlive</code> to <code>false</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"67\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerIsAlive = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerIsDefeated = !playerIsAlive;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerIsDefeated);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>playerIsDefeated</code> followed by <code>=</code> and then <code>!</code>, <code>playerIsAlive</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145220,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does the <code>!</code> operator do?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">It turns <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> values into their opposite</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">It checks if values are equal</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It turns <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> values into their opposite.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145221,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code display <code>false</code> in the console?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" canRespawn = !\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(canRespawn);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The <code>!</code> operator in front of <code>true</code> turns its value into false</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Variables always display as <code>false</code> in the console</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The <code>!</code> operator in front of <code>true</code> turns its value into false.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145222,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we call the <code>!</code> sign in front of <code>true</code> or <code>false</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The <code>!</code> sign is the negation operator</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The <code>!</code> sign is the addition operator</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The <code>!</code> sign is the negation operator.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145223,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which value does <code>result</code> store?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = !\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>false</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>true</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>false</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145224,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use the negation operator and store a value in the variable.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"31\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemySpawnEnabled = !\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!</code>, followed by <code>true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145225,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Display <code>false</code> in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!false\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"17\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(!\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>!true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145226,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the variable and save the negated value in it.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option startIndex=\"31\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"57\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" doorIsOpen = \" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" doorIsClosed = !doorIsOpen;\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>doorIsClosed</code>, and finally <code>!doorIsOpen</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145227,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code <code>!true</code> inside the display statement.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"17\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(!\" /><text value=\"true\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\");}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>!true</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}